### Create-or-replace (#105), against real PostgreSQL in the container.
###
### RUNS LAST, after 110-Batch, for the reason that suite gives: every suite pinned to 010-Seed's row
### shape has already run, so the rows written here cannot change an answer somebody else is measured
### against.
###
### The in-process suite proves what a replacement IS — the branch, the write check on both sides of it,
### the whole-row semantics. Only the real stack can show the two things below: that the id a client
### chose really becomes the row's primary key on PostgreSQL, and that `access_code` — declared
### `required` AND `hidden` on work_orders — makes this entity genuinely un-replaceable for a caller who
### cannot read it back. That field is the reason the case exists at all; a synthetic entity would prove
### the code path and not the problem.

### A PUT on an id nothing holds creates the row under that id
# @name ReplaceCreates
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
PUT {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/8f2a1c40-5d3e-4b91-9a77-2c6e0b4d1f01
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reference": "WO-3001",
  "title": "Replaced into being",
  "description": "A description this row starts with",
  "status": "scheduled",
  "priority": 2,
  "access_code": "ACME-3001",
  "customer_id": "{{CustomerAcmeId}}",
  "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}"
}

### The same PUT again, on the row it just created: replaced, not created
# @name ReplaceReplaces
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
PUT {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/8f2a1c40-5d3e-4b91-9a77-2c6e0b4d1f01
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reference": "WO-3001",
  "title": "Replaced again",
  "status": "scheduled",
  "priority": 2,
  "access_code": "ACME-3001",
  "customer_id": "{{CustomerAcmeId}}",
  "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}"
}

### The row as it now stands, read back — the description the second body omitted must be gone
# @name ReadReplaced
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/8f2a1c40-5d3e-4b91-9a77-2c6e0b4d1f01
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### A body omitting `access_code`, which is required and hidden: refused, naming the field
# @name ReplaceWithoutTheSecret
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
PUT {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/8f2a1c40-5d3e-4b91-9a77-2c6e0b4d1f01
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reference": "WO-3001",
  "title": "No access code",
  "status": "scheduled",
  "priority": 2,
  "customer_id": "{{CustomerAcmeId}}",
  "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}"
}

### And PATCH on the same row with the same omission is fine, which is what makes the refusal above
### a statement about PUT rather than about the field
# @name PatchWithoutTheSecret
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
PATCH {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/8f2a1c40-5d3e-4b91-9a77-2c6e0b4d1f01
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Patched without the secret" }
